        <mxCell id="c72" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined: the MAD column (teal) and the partial-payment row (coral). The values are Tutorial 8.1&#x27;s: all payments 0.01295, marginally acceptable conformity; full payments (Amount = GrandTotal) 0.00755, acceptable conformity; partial payments 0.04496, nonconformity, plausibly because only invoices of $1,000 or more are paid in parts (the smallest, $1,000.24), a selection by size. Each group has 9 digits, so none is missing. The editor is scrolled to the last branch of the Groups CTE, the Observed CTE and the final SELECT.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="688" width="860" height="72" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
